A||N||18||shawnster84||Don't buy from Autozone!!||||8||
Z||000000||shawnster84||10-02-2001||07:10 PM||||They really stuck it to me!! I bought a rack and pinion from them($114.00) and installed it and it looked like it had a little play in it so I removed the plastic boot on the pass side and a bunch of water dripped out of it(I don't drive this car in the rain, and its stored in a climate controlled garage) the inner control arm is rusted to hell and the bushing thats in the rack has a lot of play in it..I'm gonna remove it this weekend and take that piece of crap back!!..It looks like all they did was put new boots on it and paint it..maybe I can get 2 inner tie rod ends and the rack bushing..that way I know it will be new..theres no way of telling what the condition is with the boot on it...BEWARE BUYER!! ||||reg||8
Z||000001||theogre||10-02-2001||08:11 PM||||It was the rebuilder that stuck you. Not AutoZone. Problems with rebuild parts are very common. There are few companies in that market that really do their best to turn out high quality work. It makes companies like A1 Cardone, who actually does turn out good work, go nuts.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||shawnster84||10-02-2001||08:38 PM||||Your right, I shouldn't blame autozone..but I just hope they try to help me out and backcharge the rebuilder.. I retract my subject heading..They are pretty cool..I can even exchange electrical parts there, no questions asked.. I was told by the guy that the rack was completely rebuilt..he didn't know..it looked rebuilt on the outside but it looks worse then the one I used for a core on the inside...They'll straighten it out..||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bluebottlejunky||10-02-2001||10:06 PM||||nods :P<BR><P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>85'GT 4sp<BR>AIM: <B>KilleRedGT</B>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Scott||10-03-2001||12:38 AM||||I work at an AutoZone.  Don't worry, they'll give you a new unit, with no problems.  AutoZone's big hook is customer service.  We always take broken/bad parts back, without question.  Sucks when this stuff happens.  We don't look at every part that comes accross the parts counter (but we probably should).  If it's a rebuilt part, we just assume that it will work as promissed.  If it doesn't, that's what the lifetime guarantee is for.  I recently put in a rebuilt rack & pinion from AZ on my '85 GT, and it's working great.  You shouldn't have any problems with a 2nd one, but look it over first.<BR>Good luck,<BR>Scott    ||||reg||1
Z||000005||ka4nkf||10-04-2001||01:25 AM||||I buy stuff at auto-zone but I don't like to.<BR>My daughter worked at auto-zone when they first started. the story is that a company known as malone & hide a large food change company had a surples amount of money that they needed to get rid of so they started the auto store known as Auto-Shack. Radio Shack sued them because the name was too close to their name. so they changed the name to Auto-Zone. Now what I am getting at Auto-Zone did pay the employees minimun wages, and I guess they still do. all the money they are making and treating the employees this way is not my way of life. I think they are the largest auto parts store in the US. My way of thinking is if i am in business and my employees help me make money then I sure am going to take care of them. just thought you would like to know.||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroFanaticus2||10-04-2001||07:09 AM||||I bought some spark plugs from AutoZone one time and the guy came back with some open packages.  I pulled out the plug and it had already been used and cleaned off half assed.<BR>He tried to pass 3 plugs off to me that were like that.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Scott||10-04-2001||10:13 AM||||Hi Guys,<BR>  I'm not trying to start a flame session here, far from it, but I do feel compelled to tell what I've experienced at AutoZone as an employee.  I don't know what AutoZone once paid it's employees, but I do know that is greater than minimum wage in most cases.  They pay according to how a prospective employee ranks on a test of automotive knowledge that is  given at the interview.  I make much more than minmum, almost twice, 'cause of my score on this test.  It's a good company to work for; all of the employees at the store I work at feel that AZ is well manged and like their jobs.  I hadn't expected to care much for my job when I got hired, I just thought that it would be a great way to get discount parts.  As of now I'm very happy to work there, and I don't see that changing in the future.<BR>  AZ is the largest parts store because they are able to buy in huge volume, and sell for less.  Also they don't price hike like other stores, which offer a discount to some customers, and then charge someone off the street almost twice that price.  <BR>  As for used or broken parts being intentionally sold as new, I have never seen this happen in any local AZs.  I do know that if this happened, and the district manager found out, feces would hit the turbine.  Anyway, I don't want to cause problems, I'm just trying to state facts that I know to dispell any misconceptions.<BR>Scott ||||reg||1
Z||000008||EdsB52||10-04-2001||12:38 PM||||I like AZ. In fact, they're my favorite fast-food part store. It seems like 'Pecker Auto Charts' (Checker Auto Parts) hikes the prices too much. As far as liability, well if you wrecked your car our realized any other damage due to a vendor part sold by any store, the store would carry some product liability. The fact that they didn't manufacture, rebuild, or otherwise work on the part has no bearing to absolution of legal liability (per a products liability lawyer I spoke with a year ago).||||reg||1
Z||000009||ka4nkf||10-04-2001||09:56 PM||||Thanks Scott<BR>I feel better now. Like I said my story was at the beginning of Auto Zone. I am glad to know they are paying a good wage and I will do more business with them. They do usually have the best price.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Haze_Performance||10-04-2001||10:08 PM||||<B>"My 2 3/4 cents"</B><P>I love Autozone... & Murrys Discount Auto. Never had a problem yet from eather. (I buy a <B><u>TON</B></u> of stuff from them both) <P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallindysig_copy.jpg">              .              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallredsig.jpg">        <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red">Classic Fiero Owners - <A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> - Pennocks Wild Rides - <A HREF="http://clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000011||fierovette||10-05-2001||10:35 AM||||Seems more pro Autozone, what is the vote on Pep Boys? AZ or PB ???||||reg||1
Z||000012||OcalaFiero||10-05-2001||11:27 AM||||When I lived in Ohio, I used Murray's whenever possible, they had great prices (Front calipers for 13 bucks). Now that I'm in Florida, I usually use Autozone and sometimes Discount Autoparts. ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Alex4mula||10-05-2001||12:44 PM||||PB has more variety on dislpay but AZ usualy is cheaper and I find their attendants more friendly.||||reg||1
Z||000014||StuGood||10-05-2001||12:44 PM||||I prefer AutoZone to Pep Boys.  Reasons? Location, location, location, as they say. There's an AZ within walking distance of my house!  And, there's an O'Reilly's Auto Parts, an Ace hardware, and a Harbor Freight store, about a mile away.<P>For Pep Boys, I actually have to drive a few miles.  My life is <B>so</B> difficult  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">...  go ahead and hate me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   ||||reg||6
Z||000015||bHooper||10-05-2001||02:29 PM||||i like Auto Zone.  they are much better than Advanced Auto.  either way, i usually shop price, and if it is close, i go with Auto Zone. <P>i really like Carquest, but cant afford their price's.  and there is an A-1 Auto parts place around here that i bought front calipers for $11 each from!<BR><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Spektrum-87GT||10-06-2001||12:54 AM||||around here, advance auto is the place to go, cheapest prices and they can order near anything. Only problem i have with them is just that... they dont keep stuff like sensors in stock, so you have to wait a few days. Pep boys is CRAZY expensive where I live(8 bucks for prestone antifreeze? no joke!), although they've been able to get hard to find parts also. I do have to say, Pep Boys customer service is WAY under advance and autozone, they sold me a bad fuel pump once and accused me of the old 'switch-a-roo' because the moronic lady called the parts department and said 'send up a fuel pump.. it doesnt matter which kind, just send up a fuel pump' so she could compare the fuel pump i was returning to the kind they carried, she sat there and said 'see, they are different lengths' if she wasnt a female i would have punched her for being so stupid, i ended up getting my money back after a long wait to talk with the store manager, who was also near clueless. never had any problems with autozone, but arent autozones franchise?<p>[This message has been edited by Spektrum-87GT (edited 10-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||SKIDMARK||10-06-2001||01:17 AM||||AutoZone is the only parts store that I've ever been to that sent me to another store (Federated)because they were cheaper and had a part I needed in stock. I usually go to AutoZone for the common stuff but the one near me doesn't carry a lot of Fiero parts. We have Forest City near here too and they are really a bunch of losers. They sell a part for $10 with a 90 day warranty or $25 with a lifetime. They don't tell you it's the same part! One guy they hired there didn't know what an ignition coil was. ||||reg||12
Z||000018||William Federle||10-06-2001||12:45 PM||||I get most of my parts from Autozone. They helped me get the Ebrake spring bracket off of one of my rear calipers and found a bolt to attach it to the replacement caliper with. They spent about 30 minutes working on it.||||reg||1
